y the peer whose reply the guard discards. Prediction from the same path: on a later startRecoveryForInstance(0,0) the local vbal token equals the tried ballot, so the COMMITTED reply is no longer adopted and the reply is counted, giving sub-case 3 (epaxos/epaxos.go:1269-1272) and an accept phase that commits the NOOP at the recovering replica while replica 2 keeps X - a completed contradiction of a committed value.\\\",\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n  \\\"The stall is not universal: replica 4 accepted and pre-accepted the recovered proposal, and the peer holding X is protected in its own state (epaxos/epaxos.go:1082), so the mechanism damages progress at the recovering replica rather than silently rewriting a committed value at its holder.\\\",\n  \\\"The stall was observed only for a restarted phase-1 proposal whose value is the NOOP that the same recovery fabricated; the run does not show a leader with a genuine client value stalling this way.\\\",\n  \\\"The peer's COMMITTED status is the target's own honest answer; the defect lies in the recovering side's handling of that answer, not in the peer's reply.\\\"\n ],\n \\\"limitations\\\":[\n  \\\"One run, one instance (0,0) with N=5, F=2 and one command; the guard's interaction was not exercised for a leader that holds its own command, nor for a lower ballot on the COMMITTED reply.\\\",\n  \\\"The harness delivered the replies and did not run the executor's timer: the repeated attempt that would complete the contradiction is predicted from source, not measured.\\\",\n  \\\"The recovering replica's instance is left PREACCEPTED, which also means the dependents of (0,0) at the recovering replica would not progress; that consequence was not measured because no execution path ran.\\\"\n ],\n \\\"joint_history\\\":\\\"Producer and result indices all belong to receipt 9b8471479d484a12bdaf961653bbbe54 for fixed experiment cbbf11dd38d843f1b6acf52fd5b6e82e-experiment and describe instance (0,0): index 11 is the live holder's