{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('draft/update10.json'))\nd['rationale']=(\\\"Interpreted the completed committed-value receipt, then extended the same probe with the executor's second recovery attempt so that the predicted completed contradiction can be measured rather than predicted; a fresh execution of the revision is requested. The value-adoption account cites both executed witnesses and the status-guard account keeps its conditional claim, whose outcome this revision now puts to the test.\\\")\nexp={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"cbbf11dd38d843f1b6acf52fd5b6e82e-question-0\\\",\n \\\"previous_id\\\":\\\"cbbf11dd38d843f1b6acf52fd5b6e82e-experiment\\\",\n \\\"revision_reason\\\":\\\"Added the executor's second startRecoveryForInstance attempt at the same instance after the first attempt stalled, with observations of the second attempt's ballot, appended replies, dispatch and the replicas' final states. The commit-before-recovery sequence, crash points, ballots and handlers are unchanged.\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"epaxos/assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n \\\"execution_package\\\":\\\"./epaxos\\\",\n \\\"test_names\\\":[\\\"TestAssuranceEPaxosRecoveryContradictsCommittedValue\\\"],\n \\\"anchors\\\":[\n  {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-decl-recovery\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"startRecoveryForInstance\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1127,\\\"end_line\\\":1141},\n  {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-decl-prepare-reply\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"handlePrepareReply\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1204,\\\"end_line\\\":1235}\n ],\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-decl-recovery\\\",\\\"s-decl-prepare-reply\\\",\\\"s-recovery-init\\\",\\\"s-prepare-reply-adopt\\\",\\\"s-subcase-dispatch\\\",\\\"s-preaccept-reply\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"Same scenario as the committed-value experiment (owner commits X, its Commit reaches only replica 2, owner fails, replica 3 - which holds no command - recovers instance (0,0)) with one addition: after the first recovery attempt completes its quiescent exchange, the harness invokes startRecoveryForInstance(0,0) at replica 3 a second time, as the executor does after COMMIT_GRACE_PERIOD, and completes the exchange again.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n   \\\"Same construction, row sizing, transport boundary and crash model as the earlier experiments in this harness.\\\",\n   \\\"The second startRecoveryForInstance call models the executor's retry (epaxos/epaxos.go:394-417); no timer is run.\\\",\n   \\\"No production logic is modified.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No client path, no state-machine execution, no run() loop or recovery timer loop in the harness.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"n\\\":5,\\\"f\\\":2,\\\"owner\\\":0,\\\"recoverer\\\":3,\\\"committed_peer\\\":2,\\\"value_ballot\\\":0,\\\"recovery_ballot\\\":8,\\\"attempts\\\":2}\n },\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"The harness repeats the committed-value sequence and then re-invokes the recovering replica's own startRecoveryForInstance(0,0), delivering every emitted Prepare/PrepareReply/PreAccept/Accept/Commit through the target's handlers and recording the second attempt's ballot, append count, follow-up message types and every replica's final instance state.\\\",\n \\\"requirement\\\":\\\"A recovery must not decide a value different from a value that another live replica has already committed for the same instance; if a prepare reply reports the instance as COMMITTED with a command, the recovery must adopt that value rather than fabricating a replacement.\\\",\n \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"The recovering replica's value adoption and sub-case dispatch (epaxos/epaxos.go:1236-1313) together with its phase-1 handling of a peer's COMMITTED status (epaxos/epaxos.go:847-895); the committed peer's reply is the target's own honest answer and the second attempt is the executor's own retry.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"live-peer-committed-value\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"instance_state\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"phase\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"after_commit\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":4},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"cmd_op\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"recovery-start\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"recovery_start\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"self_has_command\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"self_status\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":0}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"committed-reply\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"prepare_reply\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":4},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"has_command\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"cmd_op\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"first-attempt-stalled\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"instance_state\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"phase\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"after_first_attempt\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"status\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"second-attempt-dispatched\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"recovery_attempt\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"round\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":2},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"instance_status\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3}]}\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"instance_state\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"replica\\\",\\\"instance_row\\\",\\\"instance_index\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"recovery-start\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"cmd_op\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":1},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"phase\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"final\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"replica\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3}],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"The value the recovering replica ends up deciding equals the value another live replica has committed (X); violated when the recovering replica ends COMMITTED with the NOOP (cmd_op 0) while replica 2 holds X committed.\\\"}\n ]\n}\nd['experiment']=exp\njson.dump(d,open('draft/update11.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission update11.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
